# .dockerignore — what NOT to send to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# `docker build .` tars up the whole directory and uploads it before a single
# instruction runs. This file trims that upload. It is not cosmetic:
#
#  1. Speed. node_modules alone is ~300MB and 40,000 files.
#  2. Correctness. The build restores packages INSIDE the image. If the host's
#     obj/ folders were copied in, they would overwrite the container's restore
#     output, and `dotnet publish --no-restore` would fail or link against
#     assemblies built for the wrong runtime.
#  3. Safety. Anything copied in can end up in a layer of a published image,
#     and deleting it in a later instruction does not remove it from the layer
#     it was added in. Keep secrets out of the context in the first place.
#
# Syntax matches .gitignore. ** matches any number of directories.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — regenerated inside the image, must not come from the host
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local-only files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/DataProtectionKeys/
**/appsettings.*.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and CI metadata — never needed to compile the app
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitleaksignore
.github/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, OS and test noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.idea/
**/*.user
**/TestResults/
**/coverage/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation and the Docker files themselves
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Excluded so that editing a markdown file does not invalidate the COPY layer
# and force a full rebuild.
docs/
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
**/Dockerfile

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data the app writes into its own source tree during local dev
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/Api/Storage/
src/Api/content/
src/Api/logs/
